   "text": "I read the molecule in six pieces and joined them into one SMILES.\n\n1. **Left end:** a pyrrolo[1,2-b]pyridazine with a nitrile on the six-membered ring. Its pyrrole carbon next to the bridgehead nitrogen is bonded to a pyridine.\n2. **Pyridine:** the carbon bonded to the pyrrolopyridazine is C2. C4 carries an isopropylamino group (NH\u2013CH(CH3)2). C5 is bonded to a 1,3,4-thiadiazole.\n3. **Thiadiazole and linker:** the thiadiazole's other carbon carries a piperazine nitrogen. The far piperazine nitrogen is acylated by a C=O that leads to C4 of a piperidine.\n4. **Piperidine to pyrrolidine:** the piperidine nitrogen is linked through a CH2 to C3 of a pyrrolidine. That CH2 is drawn on a hashed bond.\n5. **Right end:** the pyrrolidine nitrogen is bonded to C5 of a phthalimide-type isoindoline-1,3-dione. Its imide nitrogen carries a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group.\n6. **Stereochemistry:** the only drawn stereocentre is the pyrrolidine C3. Ranking its substituents gives ring C2 (next to N) first, the exocyclic CH2 second, ring C4 third and H last. With the CH2 hashed, so that H points toward the viewer, the arrangement is R. I wrote this as `[C@H]` in the SMILES order used here. I worked out the chirality symbol by hand and did not run it through a toolkit.\n\nSMILES: N#Cc1cnn2c(-c3cc(NC(C)C)c(-c4nnc(N5CCN(CC5)C(=O)C5CCN(CC5)C[C@H]5CCN(C5)c5ccc6c(c5)C(=O)N(C5CCC(=O)NC5=O)C6=O)s4)cn3)ccc2c1"
